            <div xml:id="d90">

                <pb facs="0199" n="75" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg75"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A4/202a: Circular telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Diplomatic Representatives in France, Great Britain,
                            Italy, and Japan</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-09-27T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 27,
                                1921—4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Conference on Limitation of Armament. Department’s circular of September
                        3.<anchor n="81" xml:id="d90-f1"/> President Harding for same reasons
                    expressed therein in case of Belgium and Holland desires now to invite the
                    Portuguese Government to Conference for purpose only of taking part in
                    discussion of Pacific and Far Eastern problems, if the Government to which you
                    are accredited has no objection. Please inquire and cable reply as soon as
                    possible.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
